-- AutoUpgradeGui (LocalScript)
-- WHERE TO PUT THIS:
--   Place this script in StarterPlayerScripts (or StarterGui — anywhere
--   that runs once per client). It builds its own floating panel — you
--   don't need to build any UI by hand in Studio.
--
-- PANEL LAYOUT: a dark "admin panel" look with a ☰ top bar and a left
-- sidebar of 5 icon + label tabs:
--   ⬆  Upgrades  — Stamina, Speed, and Carry merged into one tab, shown
--                   as three stacked stat cards (buy 1 level / auto-buy).
--   🧭 Teleport   — spin through all 10 rarity zones and jump straight
--                   there, using hardcoded coordinates (no streaming
--                   dependency), plus a "Save Spot" button as a manual
--                   override for any zone whose position doesn't match.
--   💰 Collect    — sweeps every "CollectTouch" slot on YOUR OWN base by
--                   briefly moving your character through each one, then
--                   returns you to where you started. A scripted
--                   alternative to the game's native Auto Collect, which
--                   is gated behind a paid gamepass
--                   (LocalPlayer:GetAttribute(...AutoCollect) == nil ->
--                   Robux prompt instead of collecting).
--   🌾 Farm       — checks zones deepest (God) to shallowest (Common),
--                   skips any zone with nothing currently spawned, and
--                   goes for the highest-earning wild brainrot in the
--                   first zone that has one.
--   ⏰ God Watch  — parks on the God zone pad and stays there (instead
--                   of patrolling), reading Workspace.GOD_TIMER's
--                   countdown if it can find one, and grabbing the God
--                   brainrot the instant it spawns.
--
-- IMPORTANT CAVEAT: server Scripts aren't included in the exported place
-- file, only client-side LocalScripts/ModuleScripts — so the exact
-- mechanics behind collecting a slot, catching a wild brainrot, and the
-- God countdown's display are inferred from part/model names and the
-- LocalScripts that DO reference them (e.g. CollectedCash, GOD_TIMER),
-- not confirmed against the actual server logic. If any of Collect /
-- Farm / God Watch doesn't actually work in-game the way it's supposed
-- to, tell me what happens (or doesn't) and I'll adjust the approach.
--
--   A small gear button in the corner reopens the panel if it's closed.

